nr-relay-turn wire fragment

No Cargo, workspace or compose_flip change is needed: mixdog-relay already depends on base64, hmac, sha1, sha2, ring,
serde_json and mixdog-js, and src/ice/ is already declared by lib.rs (`pub mod ice;`).

What the wiring (the legs task that handles the desktop leg's `ice-servers` request, and the server start) must apply:
- Start: `mixdog_relay::ice::turn_config_from_env(&config.env)`. Ok(Some(c)) -> `IceService::new(c)`. Ok(None) -> no service, no
  ice capability. Err(e) -> `logline::emit(&logline::turn_issuance_disabled(&e.to_string()))` and no service.
- Request (`requestIceServers` of lib/ice-legs.mjs): requestId must be a routing id; no clients for the device ->
  `refusal_reply(id, IceRefusal::NotPaired, None)`; `!service.limiter.allow(device)` ->
  `refusal_reply(id, IceRefusal::RateLimited, Some(service.limiter.retry_after_ms(device)))`; else
  `IceService::issued_reply(id, &service.issue(device, rate_limit::now_ms()))`. Log lines as ice-legs.mjs writes them
  (`[relay] ice-servers refused cause=<IceRefusal::name()> device=<first 8 units>` / `issued`).
- Nothing to remove from SERVICE_PENDING by this task.
